setpage('3066','7.A-1 Pro Analytics Setup and Quick Start',
 P('Use this guide to prepare a company workspace for reporting. Owners manage company connections; team members use the access they have been given. You do not need to create a developer application, set up a separate server or install the old SMM weekly reporting plugin on the customer website.')+
 H('1. Confirm the Company')+P('Open Pro Analytics. Choose the intended company and check its name and logo. If you manage more than one company, use the company switcher whenever you change clients. Connecting a provider while viewing one company must not be assumed to connect another.')+
 H('2. Complete Company Details')+P('In Account → Company, save the website, logo, social profile links and intended service area. Saving these details does not authorize an API connection or apply geography filtering. Use full city/state/country information for the market record.')+
 H('3. Connect Website Analytics')+P('The Owner uses the Google connection control in Account, signs in to a Google account with access to the intended GA4 property and selects that property. Confirm the connected property after returning. If the intended property is missing, obtain access from its administrator rather than selecting another client’s property. Your website administrator must separately verify that GA4 tracking and the relevant events are installed and collecting.')+
 H('4. Select Email Provider')+P('Choose Mailchimp or Constant Contact if your company uses it. Complete the provider-specific authorization or credential fields shown in Account, select the appropriate audience/account and save. Enter any required credential only in the intended secure settings field. Confirm the displayed connection status; do not repeat a completed setup merely because you have returned to the page.')+
 H('5. Connect Facebook and Instagram')+P('The Owner authorizes the Facebook account that can manage the intended Page, grants the requested reporting access and selects the correct Page. For Instagram reporting, use the supported professional account linked to that Page and authorize its required reporting permissions. Confirm the actual Page/account names. A social profile URL alone is not a connection, and one successful client connection does not authorize every client.')+
 P('If a Page or professional Instagram account is unavailable, check the authorizing person’s access, the Page/account linkage and the provider approval message. Some customer connections may require provider approval before they can be used. Do not substitute another company’s account.')+
 H('6. Invite the Team')+P('Use Account → Users and Invite. Give the recipient the appropriate role and explain what you want them to review. Owners manage the company; Analysts can analyze and request new Reviews when enabled; Viewers can read shared reporting. Analytics-only invitations do not enroll someone in Live Campaign courseware.')+
 H('7. Verify and Run a Report')+L(['Confirm the company and provider identities.','Verify configured form and phone events.','Select a period with known data and choose None, Prior period or Previous year.','Apply dates and wait for the completed report. Read the visible status if a provider is unavailable.','Inspect Report sections, then Print / Save a baseline.','Upload a Strategy Canvas or Brand Dyno document in Account if available before a new Pro Analytics Review.'],True)+
 H('When Something Is Missing')+P('Check the company, property, date range, provider status and permissions first. Missing history, a new tracking installation or a restricted demographic result is not the same as zero performance. If you need support, share the company name, selected dates and visible error—not a secret, access token or private invitation link.'))

